            "review_title": "Review at Hai San 79",
            "review_text": "Jordan F\n2 contributions\n0\nTourist trap colluded with taxi driver. Stay away\nFeb 2024 • Friends\nDO NOT GO. A tourist trap. Wish I read other reviews here ahead. (Skip those reviews from vietnam names). We originally booked a seafood restaurant elsewhere. The cab driver we hired for the day (one of the blue cab company as told by resort) insisted we must not go claiming it was way overprice for tourist. After a long conversation, the cab driver took us here instead. \n\nTurned out this was outrageous and very seriously overpriced! Bill was way higher than the quoted. Deliberately deceptive. \nA medium crab, one <2 lbs lobster and a plate of fried small clams, 3 small steamed uni (which were really only steamed egg white with barely any uni) in this small vietnam store came to about CAD $360+ \nWhile the taste of crab and lobster were fresh. Uni was not good at all. The seats and table were very uncomfortable. Hygiene was bad. The washroom was very dirty and the sink faucet barely had water. Most of all, it is NOT the price range in vietnam for similar seafood dishes. They definitely jack up the price for tourist. (And our cab driver had an excuse to bail out early before we got the bill and finished last ride of the day. Probably to avoid our complaint from this set up)\n\nBe Careful and Stay Away!\nRead more\nWritten February 20, 2024",
